---
name: sdh-cross-repo-announce-read
description: >
  Use at session start to process unsolicited announcements that arrived from
  another repo — a client reads from its server, a parent server reads from its
  microservices (ANNOUNCE-NNN.md files in docs/server-announcements/ or
  docs/microservice-announcements/). Covers scanning the folders, integrating,
  acknowledging by deleting the file, and committing. To PUSH an announcement
  yourself — skill sdh-cross-repo-announce-send.
---

An announcement arrived: a push from another repo that needs your reaction and expects no answer. Pushing one yourself → `sdh-cross-repo-announce-send`; a `REQ-*.md` arrived → `sdh-cross-repo-req-answer`.

## When

At session start **and** at every release closure (a long session outlives an arrival).

## Where

- Client → `docs/server-announcements/<sender>/`.
- Parent server (including a microservice with its own microservices) → `docs/microservice-announcements/<sender>/`.
- Every role → also the peer channel `docs/InOutBox/inbox/<peer>/` and `pact/<peer>/` (`sdh-peer-channel-answer`) — nothing else surfaces a peer NOTE.

## Each `ANNOUNCE-*.md`

1. Read it and apply what "What you need to do" requires.
2. An announcement introducing a new error code or status: test that exact code against your handler, even if it says "keep your current check" — an equality predicate silently routes a new code elsewhere.
3. Delete the file — deletion is the acknowledgement; there is no receipt and no ✓.
4. Commit the deletion together with the changes it caused.

Deleting it yourself is allowed: the app does not track or restore announcements. Never keep a processed one — it reads as unprocessed next session.
